<title>NIGER: Niger yr-on-yr inflation falls to 3.6 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Niger yr-on-yr inflation falls to 3.6 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>NIAMEY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in Niger rose by 0.7 percent in May compared with 2.2 percent in April, cutting the year-on-year inflation rate from 4.3 percent to 3.6 percent, the government Statistics Department said.</p>
<p>					  May		April</p>
<p>	Change on month	     +0.7 pct	 +2.2 pct</p>
<p>	Change on year		+3.6 pct	 +4.3 pct</p>
<p>	Change so far in '97	+4.4 pct	 +6.1 pct</p>
<p>	Index (base 1989 = 100)   154.2	    148.8</p>
<p>The rise is due essentially to an increase in the price of food (+1.6 pct), particularly fish and vegetables.</p>
<p>The government is aiming to hold inflation below four percent this year.</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsrooms +225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
